  "scope": "Fixed-view local paring task, independent station placement/foreground ownership and live lifecycle. No seamless loop, moving contacts, cross-direction family, economy or production-ready approval.",
  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "All eight native poses retain canonical balding red-shirt Cook, brown beard, stained pale leather-strapped apron, stocky legs and capped boots. One common projected body extent; actual native boot-stance midpoints correct irregular source gutters. No moving sole, standing direction or hidden anatomy acceptance.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "Separate persistent potato block uses same520-body-height/[320,616] basis as actor. Native boot roots are stable after whole-pose registration. All eight layered views and actual day2 arrival at-3.5/4.5 reviewed; both meal blocks stay after cancellation/departure/day resolution. No furniture pixels are in the actor source.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "One knife stays in anatomical right hand and same potato in left throughout. Blade starts on skin0, starts curl1, passes through distinct stroke2/3, completes lower stroke4, lifts5, recovers6 and holds clear7. Source-bound hand/knife/potato/ribbon contours retain lower stroke above tabletop. The first behind-table-only composition was rejected; no limb pixels are edited or duplicated.",
    "prop-continuity": "Single attached skin ribbon grows through stroke1-4 and stays attached to same held potato through5-7. Exposed yellow patch persists. No imaginary drop, duplicate potato, disappearing strip or bowl transfer. Station owns static bowl/skins/loose potatoes; actor owns knife, held potato and ribbon. One finite paring stroke, not a completed whole-potato processing loop.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Actual day1/day2 meal jobs expose each of eight authored-duration poses, complete once, hold7 for5000ms without another operation, release on cancellation/day resolution, and reset0 only on explicit reassignment or morning. A daily operation chooses its own physical task target; renderer never awards inventory/economic output."
  },
